  ' ============================================================
  ' CONTRIBUTION (anchor type)
  ' ============================================================

  class Contribution <<engine,record>> {
    +id: String
    +panel: String
    +slot: String
    +value: JsonObject
    +targetIdentityKey: String
    +contributorKsId: URI
    +kind: ContributionKind
    +checkpointId: String
    +determinism: Determinism
    +cacheKey: String
    +derivedFrom: List<String>
    +supersedes: List<String>
    +createdAt: Instant
  }

  enum ContributionKind {
    KS_DERIVED
    INSTRUCTIONS_DERIVED
    USER_OVERRIDE
  }

  enum Determinism {
    DETERMINISTIC
    NON_DETERMINISTIC
  }

  note bottom of Contribution
    **Contribution** — Atomic post on the Blackboard.

    **Concept Semantics**:

    - The unit of work on the Blackboard. Posted by a Knowledge
      Source (or by the Initializer for `INSTRUCTIONS_DERIVED`, or by
      a Reviewer at a Checkpoint for `USER_OVERRIDE`).
    - Belongs to exactly ONE `(panel, slot)` pair, where
      `slot` is a key in the panel's `slots`
      map. The Contribution is HELD in that slot's `contributions`
      list (composition is the navigational truth); the `panel` and
      `slot` fields here are wire identifiers / back-references used
      for serialization, dispatch, and audit.
    - The engine attaches `id`, `contributorKsId`, `kind`,
      `derivedFrom`, `createdAt`, `supersedes`. KSs cannot fabricate
      them.
    - User overrides cascade via the Override Cascader: cascade scope
      is the closure over `derivedFrom` UNION all downstream panels
      for the same `targetIdentityKey` (I-11).

    **Field Semantics**:

    - `kind`: provenance class — `KS_DERIVED` (default),
      `INSTRUCTIONS_DERIVED` (Initializer-posted before Control
      starts), `USER_OVERRIDE` (Reviewer-posted at a Checkpoint).
    - `checkpointId`: required when `kind = USER_OVERRIDE`.
    - `determinism`: `DETERMINISTIC` (structural extraction) or
      `NON_DETERMINISTIC` (LLM-driven).
    - `cacheKey`: required when `determinism = NON_DETERMINISTIC`
      (I-4). Stable hash of `(KS id, KS version, all read inputs)`.
    - `derivedFrom`: ids of Contributions read by the KS to produce
      this one. Used by the Override Cascader.
    - `supersedes`: ids this Contribution supersedes (engine-set).

    **Validation Rules**:

    - `(panel, slot)` MUST be a registered pair:
      `slot` is a key in the named panel's
      `slots` map; `value` MUST validate against the
      JSON Schema bound to that key.
    - `targetIdentityKey` is required when the named panel has
      `kind = TARGET_DEFINITION` (target panels are
      identity-keyed); MAY be omitted when
      `kind = SOURCE_ANALYSIS`.
    - `determinism = NON_DETERMINISTIC` ⇒ `cacheKey` MUST be present
      (I-4).
    - `kind = USER_OVERRIDE` ⇒ `checkpointId` MUST be present
      (I-11).
  end note

  ' ============================================================
  ' SOURCING RUN CONTEXT (engine run state)
  ' ============================================================

  package "Engine run state\n(distinct from the Blackboard)" as ERS {

    class SourcingRunContext <<engine,record,immutable>> {
      +runId: String
      +profile: JsonObject
      +instructionsPayload: JsonObject
      +scope: Scope
      +focus: Focus
      +runInvariants: RunInvariants
      +resolverOverrides: Map<String, ContributionResolver>
      +externalToolBindings: List<ExternalToolBinding>
    }

    note bottom of SourcingRunContext
      **SourcingRunContext** — Frozen run-scoped engine value (NOT a
      panel).

      **Concept Semantics**:

      - Built by the `Initializer` in five substeps: Plug-in Loader →
        Instructions Provider → Scope Builder → Focus Builder →
        freeze `SourcingRunContext` → Blackboard Builder. The freeze
        happens BEFORE the Blackboard Builder stands up the panels,
        so the Run state is fully determined before any KS can run.
      - Read by all KSs as a read-only value via
        `controlContext.runContext()`. The deliberate departure from
        Hearsay-II: the Run input lives HERE, not as a Blackboard
        hypothesis (I-1).

      **Field Semantics**:

      - `profile`: operator-supplied profile (free-form Pack-typed).
      - `instructionsPayload`: forwarded verbatim from RunConfig to
        the Pack's Instructions Provider.
      - `scope`: derived `{ inclusion[], exclusion[], axisDecision }`.
      - `focus`: derived `{ priorityBands[] }`.
      - `runInvariants`: `{ maxIterations, quiescenceThreshold,
        determinismMode, completionPredicate? }`.
      - `resolverOverrides`: per-panel resolver overrides.
      - `externalToolBindings`: operator-narrowed bindings of the
        Pack's `requestedExternalTools[]` to host paths.

      **Validation Rules**:

      - Frozen after Initialization. Any mutation attempt MUST raise.
      - `runInvariants.completionPredicate`, when set, MUST resolve
        to a loadable Java class implementing the engine's
        `CompletionPredicate` interface.
    end note
  }

  ' ============================================================
  ' RELATIONSHIPS
  ' ============================================================

  ' Panel <-> Contribution
  Panel ..> Contribution : <<accepts>>

  ' Target-side DAG (engine-owned panel instances)
  DefinitionPanel --> ArchetypePanel
  ArchetypePanel --> StatementPanel
  StatementPanel --> GranularityPanel
  StatementPanel --> EvidencePanel
  EvidencePanel --> ConfidencePanel

  ' Engine run state -> Blackboard (built BEFORE panels)
  SourcingRunContext ..> Panel : <<frozen before\nBlackboard Builder>>
}

@enduml
